WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.920
"Spider-Man: No Way Home" may be&nbsp;
the most secretive movie in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.000
Marvel Cinematic Universe since&nbsp;
"Avengers: Endgame." For months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.080
it's been surrounded by rumors of returning&nbsp;
Spider-Men from different timelines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.520
villainous resurrections, and more multiversal&nbsp;
shenanigans than you could shake a Time Stone at.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.440
Star Tom Holland told Variety his third outing&nbsp;
as the famous webslinger is going to be "the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.520
ambitious standalone superhero movie ever made"&nbsp;
-- and so far it's shaping up to be just that.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.360
Here's everything we know about the release date,&nbsp;
cast, and plot of "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.480
"What just happened?"

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.360
Let's start with something we do know for&nbsp;
sure. "Spider-Man: No Way Home" is set to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.360
debut in theaters on December 17, 2021.&nbsp;
When it comes to the film's future on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.200
at-home streaming services, though,&nbsp;
things get a little more complicated.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.120
If you're an MCU or Disney fan, you've&nbsp;
likely already taken advantage of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:06.000
fact that the studios have been releasing some&nbsp;
of their most hotly anticipated blockbusters on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.280
Disney+ during the COVID-19 pandemic. It would&nbsp;
make sense for "No Way Home" to follow suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.920
except that the "Spider-Man" movies are&nbsp;
actually Sony properties, and the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.360
the character was introduced into the MCU&nbsp;
at all is kind of a business deal miracle.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.240
That deal means we get to see Holland's Peter&nbsp;
Parker palling around with the likes of Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:31.440
Strange, but it also means that you won't be&nbsp;
seeing the movie on Disney+ Premier Access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.920
That's the bad news. The good news is that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.120
is probably the only MCU movie where&nbsp;
Tom Hardy's Venom just might show up.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.440
According to "What's On Disney+," "No Way&nbsp;
Home" will be heading to Starz after its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.800
theatrical and home video runs. While it will&nbsp;
eventually find its way to the Disney+ library,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.880
that won't be happening anytime soon.&nbsp;
If you want to see "No Way Home" when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.360
premieres on December 17 you're going to&nbsp;
have to mask up and head to the theater.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.960
"Disinfect the mask."

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.320
When it comes to the cast for "Spider-Man: No Way&nbsp;
Home," there are some things we can be sure of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.200
Tom Holland is definitely back as Peter&nbsp;
Parker, Zendaya will reprise her role as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.360
MJ, Jacob Batalon will return as Ned, and&nbsp;
Marisa Tomei will once again play Aunt May.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.840
Additionally, we know that there will be&nbsp;
several crossovers with the established MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.400
"Doctor Strange's" Benedict Cumberbatch and&nbsp;
Benedict Wong will be making appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.680
while perennial MCU ensemble member Jon&nbsp;
Favreau will once again play Happy Hogan.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.960
"Happy, is that you?"

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.400
"Is it me? Yeah, of course it's me!"

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.320
Now for the really fun stuff.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.240
As has been speculated for some time,&nbsp;
there will be returning characters from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.520
Sam Raimi's "Spider-Man" trilogy and the two&nbsp;
"Amazing Spider-Man" films from Marc Webb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.480
The "No Way Home" trailer gave us a glimpse&nbsp;
of Alfred Molina as Otto Octavius, aka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.400
Doctor Octopus aka Doc Ock and with the&nbsp;
November 16th release of the final trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.040
we can now say for sure that Jamie&nbsp;
Foxx's Max Dillon, a.k.a. Electro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.840
and Willem Dafoe's iconic Green Goblin&nbsp;
are returning to the big screen.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.960
"You know how much I've sacrificed?!"

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:12.240
The trailer also showed us that The Amazing&nbsp;
Spider-Man series' Lizard and Spider-Man 3's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.200
Sandman are making a sinister return as well.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.560
J.K. Simmons, who popped up in the&nbsp;
mid-credit sequence of "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.480
Far From Home," will also be&nbsp;
returning as J. Jonah Jameson.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.160
"I want Spider-Man!!!!"

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.880
The biggest question that's been surrounding&nbsp;
"No Way Home" is whether any of the previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.120
Spider-Men — Tobey Maguire and Andrew&nbsp;
Garfield — will be featured in the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.360
Everyone from Holland to Garfield to Kevin Feige&nbsp;
himself has thrown cold water on those rumors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.280
but we know better. This multiversal crossover is&nbsp;
almost definitely happening, and even if we don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.640
get any official word on their appearance, they&nbsp;
pretty much have to be there or fans will revolt.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.720
"You have to remember, just, stay calm."

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.160
As far as the plot for "Spider-Man:&nbsp;
No Way Home" is concerned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.800
there's a lot we do know, but even more we don't.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.960
Based on the trailer and the official&nbsp;
bits of synopsis that have come out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.240
we know that the film will see Peter&nbsp;
Parker dealing with the aftermath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:15.520
of the mid-credit sequence from "Far from Home,"&nbsp;
where Jameson played a video from Quentin Beck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.120
a.k.a. Mysterio, revealing to the world that&nbsp;
the plucky high schooler is in fact Spider-Man.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.040
When the pressure of this revelation gets&nbsp;
to be too much for him, Peter goes to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.160
old buddy Doctor Strange to have him perform a&nbsp;
little timeline magic and zap everything back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.440
to before his identity was doxxed. But of&nbsp;
course, that doesn't exactly go as planned.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.400
The trailer's world-bending action and the&nbsp;
presence of villains from the previous film series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.200
suggest that "No Way Home" will see Peter and&nbsp;
his allies dealing with a total multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.400
meltdown. Of course, exactly what that entails&nbsp;
will be revealed when we see the movie itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.240
Considering this is the last movie in&nbsp;
Holland's "Spider-Man" trilogy, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.280
it's safe to say that the stakes will be huge.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.880
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"&nbsp;
hits theaters on December 17.

